const body = "Day boarding gives students a longer, supervised school day, and parents the peace of mind that their children are busy with useful activities in safe hands. Children go home every evening, so they keep family time, festivals and parental care.\n\n### What day boarding includes\n\n- Day meals, health care and sports facilities, with safety and security throughout.\n- Time for self-study at school.\n- Close contact with teachers and personal mentoring.\n- Coaching and school on the same premises, so students can prepare for JEE, NEET, NTSE, Olympiads and NDA alongside school studies.\n- Study material for competitive exams and school exams (NCERT, CBSE), prepared under the supervision of the Baluni Classes directors.\n- Daily assignments, doubt-clearing sessions on alternate days, and monthly career counselling sessions.\n\n### Why parents choose it\n\n- Working parents know their children are supervised for the whole day.\n- It costs less than residential boarding: there is no extra cost for living or food.\n- Students avoid the gap between the school syllabus and a separate coaching syllabus, and the time lost travelling between them.";
